{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires","id":1473084,"title":"Animal blood is bland or unpleasant for vampires?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-23T10:46:14-08:00","id":1473084,"title":"Animal blood is bland or unpleasant for vampires?","content":"I was reading a very old module, Ashes to Ashes. About feeding from cows, the text says: &quot;It tastes good but bland, and human blood is much more appetizing&quot;. It compares it to eating simple porridge compared to feasting on delicacies ( human blood ).<br /> Other sources describe animal blood as utterly disgusting.<br /> <br /> Well... it's not the same thing.<br /> Definetly, it's not.<br /> <br /> Bland porridge can still be moderately pleasant, expecially if one never tasted anything better. An actively unpleasant food is a source of suffering.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, in your opinion, feeding on animal blood is, for a vampire is like the life of a monk ( humble and bland ) or the life of a flagellant ( actively unpleasant an painful )?<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> ( secondary questions )<br /> ( I was thinking about a distopic settings were vampire population exploded and reliable sources of sustenance must be developed )<br /> <br /> * The blood of OGM pigs ( modified with human DNA ), more similar - genetically - to human blood, would taste better? Mabye also be more nourishing?<br /> * Animal blood laced with a small quantity of morphine and/or alchool could ameliorate the taste?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T13:42:57-08:00","id":1473105,"title":"","content":"I actually make this a point with Generation. My house rule interpretation is the following:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Thin Bloods</b> find Animal Blood appetizing and pleasant. It is not only entirely possible to subsist on animal blood as a Thin Blood but <i>easy. </i>As such, they are the only vampires who have a semi-decent chance of remaining &quot;good&quot; people no matter what.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>13th, 12th, and 11th generation vampires </b>find animal blood nutritious but bland. I wouldn't even say porridge without sugar but drinking a protean shake. Vampires of this generation pretty much use animal blood as a means of slaking their hunger and fuel. It's very useful and can prevent you from frenzying. It's also something said vampires drink en masse in order to heal injuries in lieu of killing someone.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>8th, 9th, and 10th generation vampires </b>find animal blood to be fucking NASTY. It's like drinking from a brown pond in the middle of the forest with leaves. It might even make you sick. Unlike 5th Edition rules, vampires CAN keep it down and feed from it with a point of willpower per scene and use it for healing or subsistence but it is a horrible experience all round.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Lower generations</b> still? Don't even think about it. Its impossible to keep it down.<br /> <br /> Human blood?<br /> <br /> Human blood is like sex and heroin for regular vampires and thus incredibly addictive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T14:07:40-08:00","id":1473107,"title":"","content":"I think the supposed need for elders to drink from vampires all stems from CbN. Helena had a unique flaw that writers and some readers found cool and it spawned a mess. I personally never change the food sources. Animal blood is bland and off putting but sustaining, human blood is yummy, Vampire Blood is gourmet. If a lower gen vampire wanted to drink animal blood only, he would acquire a taste for it like a human does beer, or scotch, or health food without sugar and salt.<br /> <br /> For me the vampire default will always be human blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T15:05:38-08:00","id":1473115,"title":"","content":"Vampires are the embodiment of murder. So in my mind, flavorwise blood is blood. However, there is a craving to commit murder that is less satisfying the further away you are from committing murder. Diablerie is best, since you are murdering a soul. After that is sucking a human dry. Then nonfatally drinking from a human. Then animal blood. In each case the blood tastes the same, but the half psychological/half mystical urge to commit murder builds more. This translates into increased frenzy difficulties, inability to regain willpower, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 01-24-2022, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T00:14:08-08:00","id":1473150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473115#post1473115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are the embodiment of murder. So in my mind, flavorwise blood is blood. However, there is a craving to commit murder that is less satisfying the further away you are from committing murder. Diablerie is best, since you are murdering a soul. After that is sucking a human dry. Then nonfatally drinking from a human. Then animal blood. In each case the blood tastes the same, the but half psychological/half mystical urge to commit murder builds more. This translates into increased frenzy difficulties, inability to regain willpower, that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Embodiment of murder...<br /> the sin of Caine, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T03:44:05-08:00","id":1473155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473150#post1473150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Embodiment of murder...<br /> the sin of Caine, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. In my mind that last bit of hunger you can't slake is a greatly simplified game mechanic representing the very complex result of you resisting the beasts desire to do what it was designed to do: murder, murder, and murder some more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T04:11:51-08:00","id":1473158,"title":"","content":"Something worth considering is that animal blood is, ounce per ounce, less sustaining that human blood. We see this in the charts for how many blood points you receive from animals. Vampires must drain four whole rats just to get a single BP, and even full grown cattle only have five. Despite the latter being much larger, and therefore having a higher volume of blood in their system.<br /> <br /> What this tells me is that, setting aside anything else about the symbolism of murder or personal taste, animal blood is just really watered down. Like a broth. At least porridge is a dense mass of carbohydrates. Drinking animal blood must be like trying to subsist on milk or whipped cream or heavily fluffed up bread. You can subsist on it, but you need to eat a whole lot more to get anything out of it.<br /> <br /> For a vampire, feeding from animals might seem like a huge chore. Chugging a great deal of it, just to get the same value from a relatively small amount of human blood. Not to mention most animals will die from it, necessitating the body be disposed of, to escape notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T13:34:51-08:00","id":1473196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473105#post1473105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually make this a point with Generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally do something similar in my chronicles, but have it more be a function of age and Humanity rather than Generation. But it's a tendency rather than a hard rule. The younger and less depraved the vampire, the more likely animal blood is merely bland rather than disgusting. As a vampire gets older and the age wears down on your Humanity, your diet becomes increasingly limited until certain Methusalehs can only drink vampire vitae.<br /> <br /> So PCs, who are supposed to be young vampires and likely start with higher humanity, have certain advantages that most of the NPCs of the chronicle don't have because animal blood is more palatable to them. And it's possible that if a PC becomes really nasty, or if the chronicle proceeds for a long time in game, that the players will begin noticing the changes in their tastes.<br /> <br /> There are other factors as well. Generation can be one of them, as are things like feeding restrictions because of Flaws or Clan Weaknesses. And I'll allow Gangrel to more easily consume animal blood since many of them are supposed to spend a lot of time in the wilderness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T14:20:07-08:00","id":1473202,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about that, the vampires from Ashes to Ashes weren't only really young ( just Embraced ), they were special. Created by a serum by a vampiric Pasteur ( yes , it's quite a crazy module, and one of the oldest ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T14:23:06-08:00","id":1473204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473202#post1473202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about that, the vampires from Ashes to Ashes weren't only really young ( just Embraced ), they were special. Created by a serum by a vampiric Pasteur ( yes , it's quite a crazy module, and one of the oldest ).</div> </div> </div> </div>Strangely, my longest running campaign was built around Alien Hunger with the &quot;vampire cure&quot; being a permanent part of it.<br /> <br /> Its a cure that kills 50-50 of the people it's used on.<br /> <br /> The question becomes &quot;How much do you want it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, of course, any vampire who does survive is now a threat to the Masquerade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-25-2022, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T22:45:28-08:00","id":1473236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473202#post1473202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about that, the vampires from Ashes to Ashes weren't only really young ( just Embraced ), they were special. Created by a serum by a vampiric Pasteur ( yes , it's quite a crazy module, and one of the oldest ).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mean Alien Hunger, and not Ashes to Ashes. But you described the story right.<br /> <br /> One thing about very early first edition VtM is that it hadn't yet decided on some hard and fast rules. It was entirely possible for vampires to become human again, for vampires to not be embraced, or not be &quot;related&quot; to the antedeluvians and have separate origins, and lots of other things that would later contradict the lore of the setting. It's just a natural part of any setting that while exceptions to the rules can make a great story, that it can very easily undermine the setting itself. So White Wolf became more and more officially strict about the presentation of the setting as time went on, and eventually stopped talking about anything that might seem an exception to the setting's main points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T05:08:01-08:00","id":1473248,"title":"","content":"Yes, it was Alien Hunger. I like this module because it describes basically normal people dealing with somthing unconceivable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473236#post1473236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you mean Alien Hunger, and not Ashes to Ashes. But you described the story right.<br /> <br /> One thing about very early first edition VtM is that it hadn't yet decided on some hard and fast rules. It was entirely possible for vampires to become human again, for vampires to not be embraced, or not be &quot;related&quot; to the antedeluvians and have separate origins, and lots of other things that would later contradict the lore of the setting. It's just a natural part of any setting that while exceptions to the rules can make a great story, that it can very easily undermine the setting itself. So White Wolf became more and more officially strict about the presentation of the setting as time went on, and eventually stopped talking about anything that might seem an exception to the setting's main points.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/EarlyInstallmentWeirdness\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.p...lmentWeirdness</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 01-25-2022, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T09:43:43-08:00","id":1473272,"title":"","content":"Editions are always tweaking and changing stuff. Personally, I think it's best to take from all over the editions based on your own tastes. 1e's way of doing things is as canon as V5's<br /> <br /> I'd say that &quot;animal blood is fine, but not as tasty&quot; and &quot;animal blood tastes like raw sewage&quot; are both true statements, depending on the vampire. Some might not mind subsisting on animal blood, despite the extra effort and that they'll never enjoy it like they would human blood. Some enjoy sipping cow blood between victims, like chewing gum for the flavour, but don't consider it a meal. Other vampires would gag and have to choke it down.<br /> <br /> For physical benefit, ease of &quot;digestion&quot; and psychological enjoyment, prey is ranked, with a rapid plummeting in quality/enjoyment; vampire &gt; fresh human &gt; stored/dead human blood &gt; mammals &gt; other animals<br /> <br /> Vampires are built to convert fresh human blood into vitae. Blood that differs is harder to convert, and has a lower yield for effort. It's all around less rewarding than feeding on healthy humans. And however many wasps you eat, I don't think a vampire can hold down haemolymph any better than a cheese sandwich.<br /> I would rule that your pig example would actually be a pretty good human substitute, aside from the missing high of the Kiss.<br /> <br /> The drug example would do nothing for the taste or the hunger/blood pool, I think, but the high might make it more worthwhile as a human alternative to the desperate. A sort of poor substitute, but a substitute all the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 01-25-2022, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T10:39:27-08:00","id":1473278,"title":"","content":"Human blood is cocaine, heroin, and the best part of sex in the form of a hot, savoury, delicious soup. <br /> Vitae makes the cocaine seem like coca, the heroin opium, and the feeling you get from it is like reaching the heavens (You very literally come closer to god when you thicken the blood)<br /> Animal blood is like... very similar to drinking blood as a human. Only you've got to down vast quantities of it and it doesn't sit right in you because there's a lot of impurities and waste product in the blood. But taste wise it's it's probably different from a 1 to 1 vampire to human taste. I think the more intelligent the beast, the closer it is to human, the more it's blood is worth and the less-awful it tastes, though chimps and pigs are still unpleasant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T11:25:53-08:00","id":1473288,"title":"","content":"And OGM pigs with a lot of human DNA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T15:48:15-08:00","id":1473301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473288#post1473288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And OGM pigs with a lot of human DNA?</div> </div> </div> </div>My opinion is that it's not the DNA that matters but the fact it came from a human. It's a magical curse rather than scientific.<br /> <br /> As a result, I had a vampire who created &quot;meat moss&quot; with Vicissitude/Thaumaturgy to make human blood find out that it was only half as nutritious as regular human blood.<br /> <br /> Though still certainly better than the alternative.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T21:54:17-08:00","id":1473313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473105#post1473105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Human blood is like sex and heroin for regular vampires and thus incredibly addictive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I like to think of human blood as a bistec instead of something that is outright sexual becuase otherwise feeding becomes an allegory of rape, and i don\u00b4t like that.<br /> <br /> You can still have erotic feeding, that is what casanova vampires do using seduction to isolate the victim.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T22:07:05-08:00","id":1473315,"title":"","content":"Back on topic I houserule that the beast does not feed on blood but on the life force of the living with blood being just and blood is just a vessel.<br /> <br /> Humans have selfawareness wich is the sauce that makes their blood have greater degree of life force than animal blood. On the other hand Vampires vitae is just purified life force making it the tastiest.<br /> <br /> If a vampire stays active too long he will grow stronger but loss his ability to extract life force from blood until eventually they start hunting their own species. This concludes wich <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The elder going into sleeping to reduce the strenght of his blood</li> <li>The elder getting killed by other vampires who fear him eating them too</li> <li>The elder finding a way to stay active (unlikely)</li> </ol><br /> That is the eternal fight Sire against childe a cycle born of the very nature of the vampires<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T22:13:51-08:00","id":1473316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473313#post1473313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I like to think of human blood as a bistec instead of something that is outright sexual becuase otherwise feeding becomes an allegory of rape, and i don\u00b4t like that.<br /> <br /> You can still have erotic feeding, that is what casanova vampires do using seduction to isolate the victim.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, by contrast, play up the sexual element of vampirism as it helps explain why so many humans voluntarily submit to the Kiss. It is something many would gladly pay vampires to do to them.<br /> <br /> Which helps explain why Herds exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T23:56:39-08:00","id":1473322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans have selfawareness wich is the sauce that makes their blood have greater degree of life force than animal blood. </div> </div> </div>If I remember well, there was a Nosferatu book who talked about alligator ghouls grew to be good servants, who achieved the intelligence of a 5 years old human - which is really a lot.<br /> And another supplement about a powerful Methuselha obsessed with snakes that Embraced cobras. She was thinking about trying to embrace a gorilla.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> About OGM pigs, I came up with this idea beacuse in these day the first successful xenotransplants pig-human has been done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 01-26-2022, 02:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T04:56:35-08:00","id":1473328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473107#post1473107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the supposed need for elders to drink from vampires all stems from CbN. Helena had a unique flaw that writers and some readers found cool and it spawned a mess. I personally never change the food sources. Animal blood is bland and off putting but sustaining, human blood is yummy, Vampire Blood is gourmet. If a lower gen vampire wanted to drink animal blood only, he would acquire a taste for it like a human does beer, or scotch, or health food without sugar and salt.<br /> <br /> For me the vampire default will always be human blood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Methuselahs thirst is horrendously stupid (on a wide scale, as an individual flaw it's fine) <br /> Generation is supposed to be something vampires crave, something attractive and enticing; not something that'll just make them hungry and miserable all the time. Reducing the effectiveness of food sources, as seen in V5, is a no-go ThisIsNotWorthIt, and IMO strongly shits in the face of the punk spirit and &quot;morality is chosen not ordained&quot; attitude of the first editions. Vampires should be <i>encouraged </i>to eat the rich, not reprimanded. Eating your way to God should be just as valid as trying to become human again (and yes, both should be largely valid, if not entirely obtainable).<br /> <br /> &quot;Animals aren't good enough&quot; works from the perspective of &quot;I have a blood pool of 40 so I would have to consume a hundred times my body weight in vile animal blood to be full and that would be an ordeal, but also I have a lot of blood in reserve so it's not like I really need to, and also I have a lot of abilities that make hunting humans easy so I'll likely never be in that predicament. Methuselah's thirst also works as misinformation and propaganda. But actually not being able to devour animals because your blood is too dense? Maybe the first four gens aren't commonly seen because they've all killed themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T08:31:09-08:00","id":1473332,"title":"","content":"Well, Methuselahs thirst is not such a big problem. Stake a vampire, feed him pig blood and drink the vitae. After two sips, captur a human, Embrace him, stake him and repeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T10:08:35-08:00","id":1473340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473332#post1473332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Methuselahs thirst is not such a big problem. Stake a vampire, feed him pig blood and drink the vitae. After two sips, captur a human, Embrace him, stake him and repeat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, unless you're on a Path, then that could seriously mess you up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T12:12:30-08:00","id":1473353,"title":"","content":"Methuselahs Thirst is silly and not well thought out, because the young vampire population would be wiped out by Methuselahs not unlike the populations of towns would be wiped out if vampires killed a person every 6 or 7 days while feeding (or worse every day like an Anne Rice novel). The Blood Bond aspect of VTM would basically demand the death of a person turned vampire or young vampire from each feeding, not just every other because the second level of the blood bond is still pretty strong. No elder is going to risk himself like that.<br /> <br /> It's even worse when people try to go by generation/blood potency. How many 4th 5th 6th 7th gen vampires are running about in a place like Chicago? That's a lot of murder to add to the total, and a lot of needless hassle. No one I play with roleplays feedings after awhile under normal circumstances. If you're a really powerful elder having an underling make a staked newborn to feed pigs blood to and drain will be no different. It just makes elders less good.<br /> <br /> I think when people finally thought about this stuff, they then just made up cheats and workarounds like 15th gens can't make blood bonds.<br /> <br /> It's like when people say appearance 7 or whatever Helena has, is so pretty it causes problems because everyone is either dangerously jealous or dangerously obsessed, but never say 5 potence 5 strength vampires are so strong they hurt people and break things by accident all the time. It's just a weird made up preference, 7 Appearance is incredibly helpful in reality much like a 5 is IRL. A 7 just means your everyone's type. Or diablerie makes you not you anymore and your actions aren't fully your own, you could even become an npc if the roll doesn't go right, because they want to slow players down who just want to drink their way to power as fast as possible (something they originally encouraged with modules), so here's an idea why it's a bad thing. I understand people coming up with things and if it sounds fun and works in your game great, but I bet a lot of these things are ignored more often than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T13:10:52-08:00","id":1473356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473328#post1473328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Methuselahs thirst is horrendously stupid (on a wide scale, as an individual flaw it's fine)<br /> Generation is supposed to be something vampires crave, something attractive and enticing; not something that'll just make them hungry and miserable all the time. Reducing the effectiveness of food sources, as seen in V5, is a no-go ThisIsNotWorthIt, and IMO strongly shits in the face of the punk spirit and &quot;morality is chosen not ordained&quot; attitude of the first editions. Vampires should be <i>encouraged </i>to eat the rich, not reprimanded. Eating your way to God should be just as valid as trying to become human again (and yes, both should be largely valid, if not entirely obtainable).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it really punk, though?<br /> <br /> Because when a higher gen lick diablerizes a lower gen vampire, they're taking their power for themselves. Which is to say, for themselves as an individual, singular. Diablerie isn't praxis, because it doesn't dismantle the systems of unequal (vampiric) power. It merely changes who has that vampiric power from the established Elder to the upstart Diablerist.<br /> <br /> To actually be punk, you would need to murder the Elder and allow <i>no one</i> to take the power of their blood. Otherwise, you're just setting the Diablerist to fill the same role as the one they killed, sooner or later. The disparity in blood potency persisting.<br /> <br /> Indeed, one can argue that Diablerie is a means whereby the system recuperates revolt by younger Kindred. Individual Elders can die, but the hierarchy remains. It's how the Sabbat operates, and the Camarilla is full of Elders who got where they are by having committed Diablerie (even if no one would openly admit to it). While the hierarchy would prefer that none of them die, they're willing to work with a diablerist (assuming destruction is not an option) in the hopes of turning them into another agent of the status quo.<br /> <br /> The point is to eat the rich, not BECOME them. Diablerie, in this light, is a metaphor for revolutionaries that become everything set out to destroy. It's the temptation to power, which is counter(revolutionary) to the principle of punk as agitation for freedom and equity.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, I would imagine escaping the vampiric curse cannot happen if you engage in actions directly in line with vampirism's core ethos. Predation, domination, and accumulation of power. Becoming a blood god sounds, to me, like the exact opposite of becoming a human.<br /> <br /> In fact, the most human of vampires, from a mechanical sense, are those farthest removed from Caine: thin-bloods, 14+ generation vampires, and revenants/dhampyr. Not coincidentally, these figures have the least amount and capacity for vampiric power. Yet because of this, they're most in touch with their former humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-26-2022, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T14:25:01-08:00","id":1473357,"title":"","content":"I still don't get where the problem is with Methuselah's Thirst.<br /> Staking a vampire and feeding him animal blood is a bad action, embracing people and turning them into Vitae farms is worse, but these actions are akin Premeditated Murder ( not serial murder because they're done for survival, not for fun ). And most Methuselah are on a Path anyway.<br /> <br /> A Methuselah has a Blood Pool ranging from 20 to 50, it means he needs to feed once three or four weeks, more or less.<br /> He can pump gallons of pig blood into a staked vampire and convert it into the Vitae he needs in a few hours.<br /> <br /> The Blood Bond fades in a year or so, he just needs to embrace and stake 20 to 30 poor souls and he's ok.<br /> <br /> Or he can embrace someone he finds pretty enough, utterly erase his mind with Dominate and then get Blood Bound to his harmless lover.<br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> Of, for high Humanity methuselah, he could find True Love, make a mutual blood bond, then love for a thousand years and love for a thousand more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 01-26-2022, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T15:07:11-08:00","id":1473359,"title":"","content":"It makes elders universally weaker than Ventrue on the run. In a running fight where an elder is burning blood to survive, he can't just find a victim he has to find a vampire to overpower while already down on blood and or health levels. It's also just not vampire like to not drink from humans. It's a really really big weakness tacked on to beings that are supposed to be the most powerful, not the most flawed.<br /> <br /> You think staking and storing/feeding (so they don't drop into torpor) 20-30 or more vampires is no big deal?<br /> <br /> What if he's facing down a pack of Lupines? Is it just game over even though he's got a lupine or one of their kin in his thirsty little hands? The not thinking it through part really comes in the number of potential food sources, and with the blood bond VTM went with, He's blood bound to only 20 or 30 vampires in a perfect world? What happens when all those bond weight him down into doing something stupid? I like it for Helena, however she is the only vampire that has it in my world, and for her it's a derangement, not a physical restriction. She's nuts.<br /> <br /> I just personally don't think it works, but the books are more in line with you so what do I know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T15:11:48-08:00","id":1473360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473328#post1473328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Methuselahs thirst is horrendously stupid (on a wide scale, as an individual flaw it's fine)<br /> Generation is supposed to be something vampires crave, something attractive and enticing; not something that'll just make them hungry and miserable all the time. Reducing the effectiveness of food sources, as seen in V5, is a no-go ThisIsNotWorthIt, and IMO strongly shits in the face of the punk spirit and &quot;morality is chosen not ordained&quot; attitude of the first editions. Vampires should be <i>encouraged </i>to eat the rich, not reprimanded. Eating your way to God should be just as valid as trying to become human again (and yes, both should be largely valid, if not entirely obtainable).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're saying that diablerists are SHORTSIGHTED in their quest for unlimited power at the cost of their humanity? You don't say.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T16:04:19-08:00","id":1473363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473357#post1473357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Methuselah has a Blood Pool ranging from 20 to 50, it means he needs to feed once three or four weeks, more or less.<br /> He can pump gallons of pig blood into a staked vampire and convert it into the Vitae he needs in a few hours.<br /> <br /> The Blood Bond fades in a year or so, he just needs to embrace and stake 20 to 30 poor souls and he's ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>One more point about the math. An elder with this feeding restriction isn't going to starve himself down to one or two blood points. He'll feed when he gets down to half at least. Letting yourself drop to empty is suicidal and asking for hunger frenzies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T20:40:29-08:00","id":1473377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473363#post1473363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One more point about the math. An elder with this feeding restriction isn't going to starve himself down to one or two blood points. He'll feed when he gets down to half at least. Letting yourself drop to empty is suicidal and asking for hunger frenzies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Methuselahs need lots of blood to dominate the world. Also, why would you starve yourself when you're powerful enough to feed with gusto?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T00:11:00-08:00","id":1473383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473356#post1473356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it really punk, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is a great argument... for why I'm right. <br /> <br /> We're dealing with Gothic punk here. CHOICE is what matters. If you've got your ancient prince on a stake ready for you to kill him, we will for simplicity's sake assert that circumstances don't allow you to show mercy; you can either devour him for his power, or lop off his head and deny his power. If his power is a great temptation, your choice matters; you killing that prince without taking his blood is a personal sacrifice. If eating him will make you hungry and miserable and further remove you from being a person... is killing him instead of eating him really a personal sacrifices? I mean, you're making the near-objectively correct choice. The &quot;punk&quot; who eats the prince in the first scenario can at least delude himself into thinking things will change when he's in charge, maybe he can actually create meaningful change when he's in power, but in the MT scenario the punk is litererally making everynight unlife significantly more difficult for themselves with the slight caveat that they're better prepared to deal with other vampires. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also from another perspective having morality ordained to you; &quot;diablerie is badwrong and worse than ordinary murder and you shouldn't do it&quot; is a slippery slope because, in vampire at least, it's a political issue. Who's the author to say what politics are good and bad? I keep thinking of the line &quot;a man chooses, a slave obeys&quot; because, y'know, a good narrative has people make choices that make sense from their perspective. Things get dicey when the author's opinions inform every decision made by characters who should have very different perspectives. By ordaining the morality of political issues, the author becomes The Man, not a Punk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T04:54:29-08:00","id":1473392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473359#post1473359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes elders universally weaker than Ventrue on the run. In a running fight where an elder is burning blood to survive, he can't just find a victim he has to find a vampire to overpower while already down on blood and or health levels. It's also just not vampire like to not drink from humans. It's a really really big weakness tacked on to beings that are supposed to be the most powerful, not the most flawed.<br /> <br /> You think staking and storing/feeding (so they don't drop into torpor) 20-30 or more vampires is no big deal?<br /> <br /> What if he's facing down a pack of Lupines? Is it just game over even though he's got a lupine or one of their kin in his thirsty little hands? The not thinking it through part really comes in the number of potential food sources, and with the blood bond VTM went with, He's blood bound to only 20 or 30 vampires in a perfect world? What happens when all those bond weight him down into doing something stupid? I like it for Helena, however she is the only vampire that has it in my world, and for her it's a derangement, not a physical restriction. She's nuts.<br /> <br /> I just personally don't think it works, but the books are more in line with you so what do I know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Methuselah has not to stake 20-30 or more vampire, he just has to kidnap 20-30 mortals and turn them into vampires, which following the OWoD rules is quite easy.<br /> He hasn't to feed them to prevent them droppin into torpor. He just have to stake them, let them all drop into torpor and feed animal blood only to the one is feeding from right now.<br /> 20-30 level 1 bonds means simply that he's very protective toward his little Vitae farm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T05:38:40-08:00","id":1473396,"title":"","content":"Personally I tend to run taste as reliant on humanity. Animal blood is typically bland but will do at high humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T08:19:25-08:00","id":1473408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473392#post1473392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Methuselah has not to stake 20-30 or more vampire, he just has to kidnap 20-30 mortals and turn them into vampires, which following the OWoD rules is quite easy.<br /> He hasn't to feed them to prevent them droppin into torpor. He just have to stake them, let them all drop into torpor and feed animal blood only to the one is feeding from right now.<br /> 20-30 level 1 bonds means simply that he's very protective toward his little Vitae farm.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an ST I'd call this pretty incestuous, and while I'd let it work for a while it would <i>definitely </i>end up being the source of some sort of major comeuppance. Players who stretch the rules deserve to get spanked because they usually neglect to fill in all the little details that make overly clever ideas like this fall apart.<br /> <br /> e.g<br /> <br /> Player Thinking:<br /> Step 1 - Make a bunch of childe vampires and torpor them<br /> Step 2 - Feed them animal blood<br /> Step 3 - ???<br /> Step 4 - Profit!!!<br /> <br /> ST Thinking<br /> Step 1 - That's amusing<br /> Step 2 - Screw them over with a million little details and unexpected problems that any sensible person could see coming a mile away<br /> Step 3 - They're proper spanked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","user":"Dogstar","date":". 01-27-2022, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T09:39:46-08:00","id":1473410,"title":"","content":"A player character is usually a Neonate or little more. If he tries the vitae farm trick, I agree that problems arise.<br /> <br /> But Methuselah are akin to demigods, insanely powerful and possessing superhuman intelligence.<br /> <br /> Anyway. The Vitae farm is done ( using a single Neonate toreador ) by a ghoul in the Gehenna module. Not even an ancient ghoul.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T00:09:10-08:00","id":1473558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473408#post1473408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As an ST I'd call this pretty incestuous, and while I'd let it work for a while it would <i>definitely </i>end up being the source of some sort of major comeuppance. Players who stretch the rules deserve to get spanked because they usually neglect to fill in all the little details that make overly clever ideas like this fall apart.<br /> <br /> e.g<br /> <br /> Player Thinking:<br /> Step 1 - Make a bunch of childe vampires and torpor them<br /> Step 2 - Feed them animal blood<br /> Step 3 - ???<br /> Step 4 - Profit!!!<br /> <br /> ST Thinking<br /> Step 1 - That's amusing<br /> Step 2 - Screw them over with a million little details and unexpected problems that any sensible person could see coming a mile away<br /> Step 3 - They're proper spanked</div> </div> </div> </div>Methuselah still only 'need' 1 blood a day to rise...but anyway, a better way of dealing with that is to mix the blood of multiple 'donors', it gets easier if you can preserve vitae with, say, Thaumaturgy but at the least you make a vaulderie blend, with you drinking from a mixed batch while bonding them all to you, it's still going to cause problems, and of word gets out then the War Packs and Anarchs are coming for you, but it's the less terrible way to do it I can think of","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T11:46:45-08:00","id":1473590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473410#post1473410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Methuselah are akin to demigods, insanely powerful and possessing superhuman intelligence.<br /> <br /> Anyway. The Vitae farm is done ( using a single Neonate toreador ) by a ghoul in the Gehenna module. Not even an ancient ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Methuselah don't possess superhuman intelligence! What gives you that idea? I'll tell you what: Methuselah propaganda!<br /> <br /> Secondly, just because one writer wrote about it in on one book, doesn't mean that anyone can flawlessly duplicate and expand the idea without trouble.<br /> <br /> Seems like, as it always is, that the real trouble is soppy STs letting poor players get away with all kinds of shenanigans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T15:21:13-08:00","id":1473600,"title":"","content":"This is why I house rule that a vampire cannot be Blood Bound by their own childer or childer's childer.<br /> <br /> While Methuselahs can commit regular diablerie, my view is its much more sensible to have them feeding on their childer and grandchilder with no ill effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T19:07:37-08:00","id":1473621,"title":"","content":"Another possibility: since many Caitiff/Thin Bloods are incapable of blood-bonding others, it stands to reason that Methuselahs with the Thirst will either capture a load of them to feed on, or offer them protection in exchange for laundering human blood into blood their new master can drink.<br /> <br /> The former, incidentally, neatly gives greater reason why the Camarilla is so adamant about hunting these &quot;trash&quot; vampires. Capturing them means they can be surreptitiously brought to Methuselahs to be farmed. If even a fraction of all Caitiff or Thin Bloods are staked by Scourges rather than killed on the spot, that would mean a fair number being available for this purpose.<br /> <br /> Actually, the second scenario also contributes to the anti-Caitiff/Thin Blood crusades. If even existing is a crime for these Kindred, it's easy to win them over into an exploitative arrangement with a Methuselah. Having to tithe some of their blood earnings to the master is better than being dusted. Though perhaps not by much, depending on the Methuselah they're working for. Some may not even be given freedom of movement, but are instead confined to compounds, with human blood brought to them for &quot;processing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T21:59:12-08:00","id":1473628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473600#post1473600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I house rule that a vampire cannot be Blood Bound by their own childer or childer's childer.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the issue of one's childer (or even further down the lineage) bonding the better generation in their lineage is something some players complain about or think shouldn't be done. There's certainly a logic to it, but there's counterarguments as well. I certainly think it's appropriate for the ST to rule in their own chronicles. It would certainly give yet another advantage to the elders which is either a good or bad thing depending on the ST.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T22:02:32-08:00","id":1473629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473628#post1473628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know the issue of one's childer (or even further down the lineage) bonding the better generation in their lineage is something some players complain about or think shouldn't be done. There's certainly a logic to it, but there's counterarguments as well. I certainly think it's appropriate for the ST to rule in their own chronicles. It would certainly give yet another advantage to the elders which is either a good or bad thing depending on the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the biggest argument for it is that it increases the fear of cannibalism among the undead. Not just diablerie but the idea your sire could end up turning you into a juice bag in their herd. That you might end up being unable to go to your own city or travel but be kept close because your sire wants you for food. They don't even need to slake the Methusaleh's Thirst necessarily but consider you just a delicacy that they have absolute power over.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T01:05:46-08:00","id":1473635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473590#post1473590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Methuselah don't possess superhuman intelligence! What gives you that idea? I'll tell you what: Methuselah propaganda!<br /> <br /> Secondly, just because one writer wrote about it in on one book, doesn't mean that anyone can flawlessly duplicate and expand the idea without trouble.<br /> <br /> Seems like, as it always is, that the real trouble is soppy STs letting poor players get away with all kinds of shenanigans</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Methuselah managed to survive for over a thousand years. Their experience make the wisest man looks like a newborn.<br /> They possess powers beyond imagination. They can influence the mind of thousands people without moving from their lair. They can bend the very laws of reality.<br /> <br /> And to answer your little remark about poor players, I would never allow a Methuselah as player character, they are simply too powerful to interact in a meningful way. They are un-living plot devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T01:18:07-08:00","id":1473636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473600#post1473600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I house rule that a vampire cannot be Blood Bound by their own childer or childer's childer.<br /> <br /> While Methuselahs can commit regular diablerie, my view is its much more sensible to have them feeding on their childer and grandchilder with no ill effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>But even more sensible would be to have Methuselah feeding from... Ordinary humans. <br /> <br /> <br /> Think about it for a moment<br /> Methuselah were more active in the ancient world<br /> Where there were far fewer people and they were far less urbanized. <br /> If Methuselah were to feed from vampires they'd basically need 1:1000 ratios and that'd be something well documented or mythologized because of how prevailent it was.<br /> It's silly<br /> <br /> Just let them feed from humans and animals like normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T07:53:17-08:00","id":1473655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473636#post1473636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But even more sensible would be to have Methuselah feeding from... Ordinary humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't that remove like 90% of the motivation of Gehenna.<br /> <br /> Or the entire game?<br /> <br /> The whole thing that Ancient vampires feeding on younger vampires is a major source of why the Elders hate the young and vice versa?<br /> <br /> The cannibalism fear is not a small part of why vampires hate each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T09:09:37-08:00","id":1473670,"title":"","content":"&quot;The End is Nigh&quot; has been a recurring human belief for millenia. People think the world is incomparably ancient, but the end is <i>soon</i>. Possibly because they don't want to imagine a world carrying on peacefully after them as if they were irrelevant.<br /> <br /> The young hate the old because they don't like vampires having power over them<br /> The old hate the young because they fear the young owe everything too them and yet still want to eat them for an increase in power.<br /> <br /> <br /> But also...<br /> Just imagine you're a 600 year old vampire. Being 600 years old, you have all the stuff. You have reason to fear that in the near future a 4000+ year old vampire will rise from torpor and take all your stuff, because she can and it'll be easy for her. Why not stoke some flames and get yourself a little resistance? Get some neonates stoked up to fight that monster for you. A wall of blood and meat. <br /> <br /> Ancients rising is a fear with rational origins, muddied by propaganda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T09:36:39-08:00","id":1473673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solomon Draak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473635#post1473635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Methuselah managed to survive for over a thousand years. Their experience make the wisest man looks like a newborn.<br /> They possess powers beyond imagination. They can influence the mind of thousands people without moving from their lair. They can bend the very laws of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>More propaganda! <br /> <br /> Seriously though, if meths were even a tenth as impressive as this they they wouldn't need all those silly shenanigens they get up to. Either they're immeasurably wise and intelligent, which makes you wonder why they act like petty tyrants, or they're not, and it's obvious that they're little more than ancient leeches.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T14:58:04-08:00","id":1473700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473084-animal-blood-is-bland-or-unpleasant-for-vampires?p=1473673#post1473673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More propaganda!<br /> <br /> Seriously though, if meths were even a tenth as impressive as this they they wouldn't need all those silly shenanigens they get up to. Either they're immeasurably wise and intelligent, which makes you wonder why they act like petty tyrants, or they're not, and it's obvious that they're little more than ancient leeches.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some methuselahs are geniuses.<br /> <br /> Some are like the (former) Prince of Berlin and are basically incredibly stupid man-children who are just too powerful to tell no too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}